  "worked_solution": "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${v}_{1}=3+4\\text{i}$ and ${v}_{2}=3-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(v-{v}_{1})(v-{v}_{2}) & =2(v-(3+4\\text{i}))(v-(3-4\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(v-(3+4\\text{i}))(v-(3-4\\text{i})) & =2({v}^{2}-(3+4\\text{i})v-(3-4\\text{i})v+(3+4\\text{i})(3-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2({v}^{2}-(3+4\\text{i}+3-4\\text{i})v+({3}^{2}-{4}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2})) \\\\  & =2({v}^{2}-6v+(9+16)) \\\\  & =2{v}^{2}-12v+50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(v)=2{v}^{2}-12v+50.$",
